extra='''<section><h2>Using the identity</h2><div class="usage-grid"><div><h3>Instagram and social posts</h3><p>Use a symbol-only profile image once the chosen direction has a clean icon cut. Keep the full name on introductory posts. Use cream fields, dark headings and a small saffron accent; show biryani photos in a separate content area.</p></div><div><h3>Packaging and stickers</h3><p>Use the full logo on the main label and a one-colour symbol for a small lid sticker. Keep flavour names and order details separate from the logo. Rich chilli colour provides a strong repeated brand cue.</p></div><div><h3>Menus and signs</h3><p>Set dish names in a clear sans-serif. Give prices a consistent alignment. Use the logo with generous breathing room on signs and avoid placing it over busy food photography.</p></div></div><p><strong>Proposed clear space:</strong> Reserve at least the height of the lowercase e on every side of the full logo. For a symbol alone, reserve one quarter of its width. Lock these dimensions after the selected artwork is refined.</p><p><strong>Working minimum:</strong> Present the full-logo PNG concepts at 240 px wide or larger; these are review sizes, not a certified minimum. Tiny avatars require a separate simplified symbol. Keep Odisha optional when the location signature becomes too small to read.</p><p><strong>Maintain:</strong> Original proportions, the chosen colour scheme, readable lettering and a flat appearance. Avoid stretching, shadows, glows, added borders or swapping typefaces within a lockup.</p></section><section><h2>Files and production status</h2><p>01–03 are editable vector SVG studies with outlined lettering. 04–06 are Nano Banana PNG images at 2048 × 2048 pixels with cream backgrounds. They are not transparent vector masters; generated colour and edge texture are approximate.</p><p>The new studies were visually checked for the brand spelling and composition. Each reads dum e / BIRYANI / ODISHA. The original SVG studies retain their existing one-colour proofs. The new concepts still need vector reconstruction, flat colour correction, small-size simplification and one-colour validation before final print production.</p></section>'''
